{
  "id": "2026-10-30-aiplatform-v1",
  "date": "2026-10-30",
  "api": "aiplatform.v1",
  "service": "Vertex AI",
  "title": "Vertex AI: Breaking Changes & New File/Batch Embedding APIs",
  "summary": "This update introduces several breaking changes by making key parameters strictly required and certain schema properties read-only. Developers also gain significant new file management capabilities for publisher models and a new batch embedding method.",
  "details": "This update introduces several breaking changes. The following parameters are now strictly required: `name` for `projects.locations.publishers.files.delete`, `download`, and `get`; `parent` and `publishersId` for `projects.locations.publishers.files.list` and `upload`; and `model` for `projects.locations.publishers.models.batchEmbedContents`. Additionally, the `aiApplication` property in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Agent` and several properties within `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1ClaudeFile` (including `created_at`, `downloadable`, `expires_at`, `filename`, `id`, `mime_type`, `size_bytes`, and `type`) are now read-only. Ensure your code is updated to reflect these new requirements and immutability.\n\nOn the feature front, developers gain significant new file management capabilities under `projects.locations.publishers.files`. You can now `delete`, `download`, `get` metadata for, and `list` files. The `upload` method for files has also been updated. These methods are crucial for managing data associated with publisher models. Furthermore, a new `projects.locations.publishers.models.batchEmbedContents` method is available, allowing for efficient batch processing of content to generate embeddings. Minor additions include an optional `idpNonce` parameter for `projects.locations.agents.create` and new schemas (`BoundingBox`, `PerfEstimationConfig`, `PerfEstimationConfigCharacterReference`) that extend the `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperiments` capabilities, along with `continuationToken` and `outputConfig` for `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1GenerateContentRequest`.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "AI/ML",
    "Breaking Change",
    "API Update",
    "Vertex AI"
  ],
